WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.600
Humiliation... we've all experienced
it at some point in our lives,

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.120
or we've done it to others, but why?

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:17.000
The point of humiliating someone
is to dehumanise them,

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:18.760
to redefine them.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:23.760
In other words, to rob them
of their self-perceived identity

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:25.920
and thus, attack their power.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.080
We see these exchanges in Parliament,

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.960
and this feeds
the cycle of humiliation

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.760
being part of our culture.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:41.720
We've normalised humiliation.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:46.040
If we feel humiliated
by our situation,

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:52.000
we seek a group of others to blame
and, unfortunately, humiliate.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:55.840
We're pack animals,

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:58.960
and so to be socially attractive
is important to us.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:04.120
have a role in our evolution.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.760
If we have committed
what could be considered a faux pas,

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.360
we show embarrassment,

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.200
and then we're less
likely to be attacked

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:13.080
by other members of the tribe.

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:15.840
This is why we blush
when we get employee of the month

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.040
or are otherwise singled out.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.240
We're saying with that embarrassment,
"Don't attack me."

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:26.320
Shame is something we feel
for something we've done,

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.880
and its purpose is similar.

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:31.160
Humiliation is done to us by others,

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:34.960
it is embarrassment
plus shame plus, plus, plus.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:39.680
And what the plus, plus, plus is
could be defined as loss of face.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:43.160
We have an idea
of who we are and what we're like,

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:44.240
and when this is challenged

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:46.840
we can experience
a feeling of being obliterated,

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.040
a sense of loss of self.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:53.360
We can even feel humiliated if a
photograph of ourselves is published,

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:56.520
and we have a different image
of ourselves than that photo.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:02.320
The photo is a threat
to how we want to identify ourselves.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:07.800
The usual scenario is the humiliator
fears being humiliated,

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:10.680
or already feels humiliated
and powerless,

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:15.840
and the way they seek to regain
their power is to take away power,

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:20.320
to harm the identity of the person
they see as their persecutor.

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:23.760
Men, I believe,
have a particularly tough time of it,

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:27.160
because all over the world they
have been socialised to be...

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:34.320
which usually means suppressing or
denying themselves vulnerable states,

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.400
as part of how
they identify themselves.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:42.280
For example, a lot of men feel
that in order to identify as strong,

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.600
they can't be seen to show...

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:51.080
This is a really difficult
self-image to live up to.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:54.480
When a vulnerability
is exposed by someone,

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:58.480
it may be that the only way that they
can regain their supposed power

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:00.160
is to resort to violence.

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:04.200
It may be this enculturation
of the macho tough guy

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:08.760
being the only desirable image
for a man, that's one of the reasons

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.200
that men are many times more
violent and aggressive than women.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.520
But, the violence rarely
ends anything.

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:19.640
It usually leads to more humiliation
and more violence.

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:21.960
We may have a hunger for revenge,

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:25.120
and humiliation
is often a part of revenge.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:29.400
But the only way to redemption
is to build up our enemies,

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:30.760
not knock them down.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:34.560
This means, for example,
giving prisoners education,

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.120
training and therapy.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.760
Not more punishment and,
therefore, more humiliation,

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:42.360
leading to more anger, more violence.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:47.760
Maybe we all need to be humiliated
about our habits of humiliation.

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:52.720
We need to readjust until we realise
we have been all too stupid,

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.280
lazy, unthinking

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:58.320
and, basically, daft, to carry on
with this winning and losing game.

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:02.680
Will we dare to be vulnerable and say
we don't know the solutions yet,

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:08.160
but humiliation, and otherwise
annihilating the enemy isn't working.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:12.960
We just might become
less susceptible to humiliation

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:17.440
if we were not so worried about
how others see and experience us.

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:21.240
Let's let go of self-image.

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:26.040
Thanks for watching.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:30.120
Don't forget to subscribe and click the bell to receive notifications for new videos.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.700
See you again soon!

